EXPERIMENT 59 – END-TO-END TICKET BOOKING TESTING USING APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to execute end-to-end testing of a ticket booking flow using the Transaction Controller.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Threads = 3, Ramp-up = 3 seconds and Loop Count = 1.
4. Add HTTP Request Defaults and HTTP Cookie Manager.
5. Add Logic Controller → Transaction Controller named Book_Flight.
6. Select Generate parent sample.
7. Add three HTTP Requests inside the controller:
   - Home page (GET)
   - Flight search (POST /reserve.php)
   - Flight selection (POST /purchase.php)
8. Add Response Assertions for all three requests.
9. Add Summary Report and run the test.
INPUT
Test Plan Configuration
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Threads	3
Thread Group	Ramp-up	3 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Request Defaults	Protocol	https
HTTP Request Defaults	Server	blazedemo.com
Transaction Controller	Name	Book_Flight
Transaction Controller	Generate parent sample	Selected
HTTP Request 1	Method / Path	GET /index.php
HTTP Request 2	Method / Path	POST /reserve.php
HTTP Request 3	Method / Path	POST /purchase.php

Parameters
- Flight search: fromPort = Paris, toPort = Buenos Aires
- Flight selection: flight = 43, price = 472.56, airline = Virgin America, fromPort = Paris, toPort = Buenos Aires
Response Assertions:
- Welcome to the Simple Travel Agency!
- Choose This Flight
- Purchase Flight
OUTPUT
Summary Report
Label	Samples	Error %
Book_Flight	3	0.00%
TOTAL	3	0.00%

Only the parent transaction is shown because Generate parent sample is selected.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to execute end-to-end testing of a ticket booking flow using the Transaction Controller, and the results were verified.
